1
00:00:03,200 --> 00:00:11,330
At dawn on the thirtieth of April, 1943, a Spanish fisherman found a body floating off the coast near Huelva.

2
00:00:11,710 --> 00:00:18,116
It wore the uniform of a British officer. Chained to it was a briefcase full of secret papers.

3
00:00:18,496 --> 00:00:24,064
The man had never served in any army. This is the story of Operation Mincemeat.

4
00:00:25,114 --> 00:00:33,020
In early 1943, with North Africa almost won, the Allies chose their next target: the island of Sicily.

5
00:00:33,400 --> 00:00:41,201
It was so obvious a target that, as Churchill is said to have put it, everyone but a bloody fool would know it was Sicily.

6
00:00:41,581 --> 00:00:45,669
The Germans had to be convinced the blow would fall somewhere else.

7
00:00:46,719 --> 00:00:53,534
The idea went back to 1939, to a naval intelligence memo written under Admiral John Godfrey,

8
00:00:53,534 --> 00:00:57,312
and usually credited to his assistant, Ian Fleming.

9
00:00:57,692 --> 00:01:04,091
It suggested planting false papers on a dead body. The memo itself called it a suggestion,

10
00:01:04,091 --> 00:01:05,513
not a very nice one.

11
00:01:05,893 --> 00:01:14,323
In 1943, two officers took it up: Charles Cholmondeley of MI5, and Ewen Montagu of Naval Intelligence.

12
00:01:15,373 --> 00:01:20,844
They needed a body that would pass for a drowned man. The coroner, Bentley Purchase,

13
00:01:20,844 --> 00:01:21,495
found one.

14
00:01:21,875 --> 00:01:28,079
Glyndwr Michael was a homeless Welshman who had died in London in January 1943,

15
00:01:28,079 --> 00:01:30,278
after swallowing rat poison.

16
00:01:30,658 --> 00:01:34,561
He had no family looking for him. He would now become someone else.

17
00:01:35,611 --> 00:01:40,547
He became Captain, acting Major, William Martin of the Royal Marines.

18
00:01:40,927 --> 00:01:48,180
His pockets were filled with the litter of a real life: love letters and a photograph from a fiancée called Pam,

19
00:01:48,180 --> 00:01:52,972
a bill for an engagement ring, a warning from his bank about an overdraft,

20
00:01:52,972 --> 00:01:55,627
and two theatre ticket stubs from London.

21
00:01:56,007 --> 00:02:00,205
Pam's photograph was of an MI5 clerk, Jean Leslie.

22
00:02:01,255 --> 00:02:09,123
The key document was a personal letter from General Sir Archibald Nye to General Alexander in North Africa.

23
00:02:09,503 --> 00:02:15,262
It hinted that the Allies would land in Greece, and that Sicily was merely a cover target.

24
00:02:15,642 --> 00:02:22,826
A letter from Lord Mountbatten added a feeble joke about sardines, to point the Germans towards Sardinia.

25
00:02:23,876 --> 00:02:29,665
Packed in dry ice inside a steel canister, the body was driven overnight to Scotland.

26
00:02:30,045 --> 00:02:35,034
On the nineteenth of April, the submarine HMS Seraph sailed from the Clyde.

27
00:02:35,414 --> 00:02:42,119
At about half past four on the morning of the thirtieth, off Huelva, her officers read the thirty-ninth Psalm,

28
00:02:42,119 --> 00:02:44,191
and committed the body to the sea.

29
00:02:45,241 --> 00:02:51,249
Spain was neutral, but full of German agents. In Huelva, the Abwehr had an officer,

30
00:02:51,249 --> 00:02:52,190
Adolf Clauss.

31
00:02:52,570 --> 00:02:57,901
Major Martin was buried in Huelva with military honours on the second of May.

32
00:02:58,281 --> 00:03:03,253
His papers were opened, photographed, resealed, and returned to the British.

33
00:03:03,253 --> 00:03:04,954
The copies went to Berlin.

34
00:03:06,004 --> 00:03:12,668
Intercepted German signals, decoded at Bletchley Park, showed that the Germans believed every word.

35
00:03:13,048 --> 00:03:17,667
A message went to Churchill: Mincemeat swallowed rod, line and sinker.

36
00:03:18,047 --> 00:03:25,315
Hitler ordered the First Panzer Division from France to Greece. Defences in Greece and Sardinia were strengthened.

37
00:03:26,365 --> 00:03:31,146
On the tenth of July 1943, the Allies landed in Sicily.

38
00:03:31,526 --> 00:03:37,183
They caught the defenders largely by surprise, and the island fell in thirty-eight days.

39
00:03:37,563 --> 00:03:47,596
Mincemeat was not the only reason, but the official historian of British deception called it perhaps the most successful single deception operation of the war.

40
00:03:48,646 --> 00:03:53,234
For decades, the true identity of Major Martin remained a secret.

41
00:03:53,614 --> 00:03:59,347
In 1998, a new line was carved on his grave in Huelva: Glyndwr Michael,

42
00:03:59,347 --> 00:04:01,851
served as Major William Martin.

43
00:04:02,231 --> 00:04:07,146
A man who had nothing in life had helped to save thousands of others in death.
